--- ============================================================
--- Onboarding template for a new client.
--- Copy this file, fill in the placeholders, run it against the database.
--- ============================================================
-
--- 1. Create the business.
---    domain: lowercase, NO "www.", NO "https://" — must exactly match
---    what their Hostinger site's Origin header will send (the storefront
---    is identified by this column, not by anything it sends itself).
-
---- Values to be uncommented ---
-
--- INSERT INTO company (name, city, founded_year, yards_served, years_experience, phone, email, domain)
--- VALUES (
---   'CLIENT BUSINESS NAME',
---   'CLIENT CITY',
---   2024,
---   0,
---   1,
---   1234567890,                   -- digits only, no formatting
---   'owner@clientbusiness.com',
---   'clientbusiness.com'
--- );
-
-    --- values to be uncommented ---
-
--- 2. Create their admin login.
---    The hash below is bcrypt("ChangeMe123!") — a real, working hash, not a
---    placeholder. Give the client this email + "ChangeMe123!" and tell them
---    to change it immediately via the admin panel's change-password screen.
---    Do not edit the hash string itself.
-
--- Values to be uncommented --
-
--- INSERT INTO admin_users (email, password_hash, company_id)
--- VALUES (
---   'owner@clientbusiness.com',  -- must match what you hand them to log in with
---   '$2b$10$BODrV.jJcaZ1LV4izj0Up.NSbCBYj2O3Ic10V4nOeQbFnUa8yEFt.',
---   (SELECT id FROM company WHERE domain = 'clientbusiness.com')
--- );
-
-    --values to be uncommented--
-
--- That's it — two inserts, and the business is live:
---   - Visiting their storefront for the first time auto-seeds a starter
---     catalog (services/plans/addons) with sensible defaults, so the site
---     never looks empty on day one — see ServiceCatalogService.fetchOrSeed.
---     They can edit/replace everything from the admin panel afterward.
---   - Their admin login works immediately at the temporary password above.
---
--- Known gap: there's currently no admin UI (or endpoint) to edit the
--- company's own profile (name, city, phone, stats) after onboarding —
--- that's still a direct-DB edit for now, since the original frontend never
--- had a "company settings" screen either. Worth adding a small
--- PUT /admin/company endpoint + settings page if this comes up often.
-
